# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Frontend (Vite) environment — CLIENT-SIDE config only.
#
# Everything here is PUBLIC: it is bundled into the browser app. The Supabase
# anon / "publishable" key is safe to expose — access is enforced server-side by RLS.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your own Supabase project's values.
# (`.env` is gitignored — never commit real values.)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://<your-project-ref>.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="<your-supabase-anon-key>"

# Optional. Not read by the app — kept as a handy reference for CLI commands
# (e.g. `npx supabase functions deploy <fn> --project-ref <this value>`).
VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="<your-project-ref>"

# Optional. Canonical site origin used when building shareable job/invite links
# (src/components/careers/ShareJobLink.tsx, HrTeam.tsx). Falls back to
# window.location.origin when unset — so leave it unset for local dev.
# VITE_SITE_URL="https://careers.lumofy.ai"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SERVER-SIDE secrets do NOT belong here.
#
# They live as Supabase Edge Function secrets (dashboard: Project → Edge
# Functions → Secrets, or `supabase secrets set NAME=... --project-ref <ref>`).
# Putting them in this file would ship them to every visitor's browser.
#
#   GEMINI_API_KEY            — the AI key (all 7 AI functions, via _shared/ai.ts)
#   INTERNAL_FUNCTION_SECRET  — authenticates function-to-function calls
#                               (auto-analyze-applicant's x-internal-secret header)
#   ADMIN_EMAIL               — optional; legacy verify-password login only
#
# SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are injected automatically by
# Supabase into every edge function — never set them manually.
#
# The full secrets table lives in docs/DEPLOY.md.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
